Now add lab functions. Insert after renderBuildCards. Let me write the code.

Lab functions details:

```js
/* ───────────────────────── SYSTEMS LAB ───────────────────────── */
function bestCropFor(typeId) {
  const bt = BED_TYPES[typeId];
  let best = null;
  for (const cid of bt.crops) {
    const p = potentialFor(typeId, cid);
    if (!best || p.netDay > best.p.netDay) best = { cid, p };
  }
  return best;
}
function potentialFor(typeId, cropId) {
  const bt = BED_TYPES[typeId], c = cropById(cropId);
  const cyclesYr = 52 / c.cycleWeeks;
  const kgYr = bt.plants * c.yieldKg * cyclesYr * bt.spec.growth;
  const revYr = kgYr * c.basePrice;
  const costYr = c.seedCost * cyclesYr + bt.spec.energy * 365 + 18; // misc water/nutrients per bed/year
  const netYr = revYr - costYr;
  const netDay = netYr / 365;
  const capex = bt.cost;
  const payback = netDay > 0 ? capex / netDay : null;
  const area = (bt.size ? bt.size.w * bt.size.d : 3);
  return { bt, c, cyclesYr, kgYr, revYr, costYr, netYr, netDay, capex, payback, perM2Wk: (netYr / 52) / area };
}
```

Wait, adding 18 misc cost per year per bed. Maybe fine. But should not be too arbitrary; energy is $/day so energy*365. Seed cost * cycles. Let's include nutrient/water allowance maybe `bt.spec.water * 8` per year? Not needed. Keep seed+energy.

Sort: potential systems by netDay descending, best = first. `best` marker.

Actual stats per system:
- `rec = state.stats.bySystem[t]`
- capex already accumulated at build.
- revenue, seedCost, upkeep.
- costs = seedCost+upkeep+capex
- net = revenue - costs
- roi = capex ? net/capex*100 : 0
- perDay = net / Math.max(1, state.day - startDay + 1)
- beds owned.

Lab systems render:
```
<div class=system-grid>
 BED_IDS.map(card)
</div>
<div class=sys-detail>
 head: icon, name, cost, badge best crop?
 principle
 specs 4 columns: CAPEX, POWER, WATER, GROWTH, FOOTPRINT, DIFFICULTY maybe 6 cells.
 best/best crop
 variants chips
 compatible crops chips
 tasks list
</div>
```
Need CSS for `.sys-crops`, maybe reuse `.variant-chips`.
Add a "SELECTED SYSTEM" label.

Cycle render:
- system chips row (6), crop chips row (only compatible).
- `lab.system` and `lab.crop`.
- table: Week | Stage | System care | Crop activity | Target
  - Stage determined by `(week-1)/cycleWeeks`, growth % e.g. end of week `Math.round(week/cycleWeeks*100)`.
  - System care: base tasks labels.
  - Crop activity: cropWeeklyTask or "—".
  - Target: "pH 5.5–6.5 · EC x–y"
- Summary top: cycle length, harvest week, expected kg/bed, seed cost, price.
- Also an "activity count" maybe.

Profit render:
- actual table (if beds 0 show dashes).
- potential table.
- "Best ROI" callout card.

Need HTML entity issues? Keep simple.

Event wiring:
```js
D.labTabs.addEventListener('click', e => { const b=e.target.closest('[data-labtab]'); if(b) setLabTab(b.dataset.labtab); });
D.labSystems.addEventListener('click', e => { const card=e.target.closest('[data-sys]'); if(card){ lab.system=card.dataset.sys; lab.crop=BED_TYPES[lab.system].crops.includes(lab.crop)?lab.crop:BED_TYPES[lab.system].crops[0]; renderLab(); } });
D.labCycles.addEventListener('click', e => { const s=e.target.closest('[data-sys]'); const c=e.target.closest('[data-crop]'); ... });
D.labProfit maybe click data-sys to open cycles? optional.
```
But `data-sys` might be used in both systems and cycles panes; separate listeners, fine. In cycle chips, clicking a system resets crop if incompatible.

`setLabTab(tab)` toggles `.active` and pane visibility and calls renderLab.
`openLab(tab, system, crop)` sets lab, calls renderLab, openModal('modal-systems'), then set tab. openModal will call renderLab if id. Let's integrate in openModal: `if (id === 'modal-systems') renderLab();`.

Need `renderLab` defined before openModal? Function declarations hoist so fine.

`openLab` should be callable before state? only when state. It can handle.

Also task calendar: open lab cycles with selected bed's type/crop.

Mobile nav binding.

CacheDom ids: add:
- btn-systems, btn-mobile-speed, mobile-nav, bed-specs, tasks-block, task-week, task-list, task-calendar, modal-systems, lab-tabs, lab-systems, lab-cycles, lab-profit, menu-upgrades.

Also `D.labTabs` etc.

